ith Q pair and it gets beaten by higher pair, we are left with ♣2 single and they lead whatever, we lose.  \n\nTherefore leading with highest single ♣2 is actually safer here:  \n- If they pass, we win next turn by playing Q pair.  \n- If they beat it with a 2, we still have Q pair to beat whatever they play next (since after playing 2, they would likely lead a low single or pair, which we can beat with Q pair).  \n\n**Final choice:**  \nPlay single ♣2 to force opponent to use a 2 if they have one, keeping our pair intact as a finisher.\n\n**Answer:**  \n{"cards": ["♣2"]}'}
